british-english: the word list Ledger checks spelling with, one word a line (UTF-8). It is
Quill's (Ledger's word-processing sibling), shared unchanged.

It is SCOWL's British English list (size 50, from Debian's wbritish 2020.12.07) without the
possessive forms ("'s"; Ledger accepts those for any word), with a few dozen words added that
documents about computers often use (footer, endnote, email, website...). SCOWL is
Copyright 2000-2011 Kevin Atkinson and others; see LICENSE-dict.txt for its terms.

Words added with "Add to Dictionary" go to Ledger.words next to Ledger, not here.
